{
  "title": "Places in town and directions",
  "note": "A (to) joins the article: a + o = ao, a + a = à. De (of, from) does too: de + o = do, de + a = da. So: Vou ao banco, Vou à farmácia, perto da praça. To ask where a place is, say Onde fica...? or Onde é...?",
  "src": {"t": "Língua da Gente, Elementary 26: Turn Right At The Third Door", "u": "https://linguadagente.coerll.utexas.edu/elementary-turn-right-at-the-third-door/"},
  "items": [
    {"c": "a cidade", "a": "the city", "d": ["the street", "the country"], "ex": "Salvador é uma cidade bonita.", "exT": "Salvador is a beautiful city."},
    {"c": "a rua", "a": "the street", "d": ["the square", "the city"], "ex": "Eu moro nesta rua.", "exT": "I live on this street."},
    {"c": "o centro", "a": "downtown, the center", "d": ["the suburb", "the corner"]},
    {"c": "o banco", "a": "the bank", "d": ["the store", "the post office"], "ex": "O banco fecha às quatro.", "exT": "The bank closes at four."},
    {"c": "o mercado", "a": "the market, grocery store", "d": ["the bakery", "the pharmacy"]},
